It follows that AB equals to AE divided by \cos (\alpha) and equals to AE inverse times \sin (\alpha).
It follows from Pythagorean theorem that AE squared minus (AE) inverse squared equals to 81.
It follows from properties of a triangle that AE equals to \sin (\alpha) divided by \cos (\alpha), which we may write as \tan (\alpha).
It therefore follows that \sin^2 (\alpha) equals to 1-1/\tan^2 (\alpha).
It follows that 1/\tan^2 (\alpha) minus 1/k^2 equals to 1 and therefore \tan (\alpha) equals to sqrt(k).
Therefore (AE) inverse equals to sqrt(81+k) and AE equals to sqrt(81+k)/sqrt(k).
